; Ps::RestoreAfterMovie() sends the VU1 microprograms through VIF1 with the DMA chain below, at
; 0x003ab970, and starts Vu1Init with MSCAL. Each MPG block loads at the VU address it specifies,
; and a program longer than one MPG block continues in the next. The entry points are
; Vu1DrawFaces and Vu1DrawEdges (PsMesh), Vu1DrawSprites (PsParticleSys), and Vu1DrawInstances
; (PsMultiMesh). The face and instance programs call the lighting program at the address in the
; batch header (Vu1LightPoint, Vu1LightDirectional, Vu1LightAmbient, or Vu1LightUnlit). The face
; clipper selects a plane by jumping into the table of four-instruction stubs after Vu1Addr074d.
; The chain ends by resetting the double-buffer base, offset, and cycle.

